<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- BIO-INT-003 owns api/features/bio-int-003/** only. No ProjectReference to
         Biolog.Api.csproj (one-way dependency, scripts/check-module-project-references.sh)
         and none to bio-idn-006 either - BIO-IDN-006's PermissionService/RoleAssignmentService
         are internal with InternalsVisibleTo granted only to Biolog.Api and its own test
         assembly, and this project cannot reference a sibling feature project any more than
         it can reference the host (same boundary BIO-INT-001 documented in its own csproj).
         The closed 11-role catalogue this story uses as its OAuth2 scope vocabulary is
         therefore this project's OWN documented copy of BIO-IDN-006's RoleType wire strings
         (see Domain/KnownRoles.cs) - a duplicated value set, not a live reference, the same
         "duplicate the minimal shape" boundary pattern BIO-DEV-003's DeviceDescriptor,
         BIO-RPT-001's DomainEventEnvelope and BIO-INT-001's own KnownRoles.cs already
         established (this is a third independent copy, not a refactor of BIO-INT-001's -
         that project cannot be referenced either).

         Tenant resolution: every method takes a plain string tenantId, same as BIO-INT-001 -
         api/Biolog.Api/Modules/BioInt003Module.cs resolves the real ITenantContextAccessor and
         passes the string down.

         No JWT/session ADR exists anywhere in this codebase (confirmed by search before
         designing - see BIO-INT-001's own csproj comment and docs/features/bio-crd-007's
         README). Service-account access tokens here are a hand-rolled HMAC-signed opaque
         string (Domain/ApiAccessTokenCodec.cs), the same shape as BIO-INT-001's
         HmacSessionTokenCodec and BIO-IDN-006's own ActorProvenanceGate HMAC precedent - not a
         JWT library dependency, so no new vulnerability-scan surface is introduced. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.ApiSecurity.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
